workaround:
Capture from a Fresh error hook; all three work identically on bun, pick one. Cleanest is the file-system error route, `app/routes/_error.tsx`:

  import * as Sentry from "@sentry/bun";
  import { define } from "../utils.ts";
  export const handler = define.handlers({
    GET(ctx) {
      Sentry.captureException(ctx.error, { mechanism: { type: "fresh._error", handled: false } });
      return new Response("Internal server error", { status: 500 });
    },
  });

Programmatic equivalent in `main.ts`: `app.onError("*", ctx => { Sentry.captureException(ctx.error, { mechanism: { type: "fresh.onError", handled: false } }); return new Response("Internal server error", { status: 500 }); })`. The middleware form from the report (`try { return await ctx.next() } catch (err) { Sentry.captureException(err, ...); throw err }`) also works but must be registered before every other `app.use`, or errors thrown by earlier middleware escape it. Do NOT rely on `captureConsoleIntegration`: it happens to catch these errors only while Fresh's built-in error page is in use, and stops capturing entirely as soon as the app defines `_error.tsx` or `onError`.

Fresh 2 on bun, middleware in app/main.ts (registered before app.fsRoutes()):

import * as Sentry from "@sentry/bun";
const sentryMiddleware = define.middleware(async (ctx) => {
  const span = Sentry.getActiveSpan();
  const rootSpan = span && Sentry.getRootSpan(span);
  if (rootSpan && ctx.route) {
    rootSpan.updateName(`${ctx.req.method} ${ctx.route}`);
    rootSpan.setAttribute("http.route", ctx.route);
    rootSpan.setAttribute(Sentry.SENTRY_SEGMENT_NAME_SOURCE, "route"); // "sentry.segment.name.source"
  }
  try { return await ctx.next(); }
  catch (err) { Sentry.captureException(err, { mechanism: { type: "fresh.middleware", handled: false } }); throw err; }
});
app.use(sentryMiddleware);

Yields name 'GET /users/:id' with source 'route' in both traceLifecycle 'stream' and 'static'. Do NOT use `setAttribute('sentry.source', 'route')`, that key is v10 and is ignored on v11.

Do not put `sentryCloudflareVitePlugin()` in Fresh's `vite.config.ts`. Keep `@sentry/cloudflare` and the DB driver external to the Fresh SSR build, then bundle the wrangler entry yourself with esbuild and the Sentry orchestrion esbuild plugin, and set `wrangler.jsonc` `main` to that output:

```js
// build-worker.mjs
import * as esbuild from 'esbuild';
import { builtinModules } from 'node:module';
import { sentryOrchestrionPlugin } from '@sentry/server-utils/orchestrion/esbuild';

const BUILTINS = new Set(builtinModules.filter(m => !m.startsWith('node:')));
const used = new Set();
const collect = { name: 'collect-node-builtins', setup(build) {
  build.onResolve({ filter: /^(node:)?[a-z_]+(\/[a-z_]+)?$/ }, args => {
    const bare = args.path.replace(/^node:/, '');
    if (!BUILTINS.has(bare)) return null;
    used.add(bare);
    return { path: `node:${bare}`, external: true };
  });
}};
const common = {
  entryPoints: ['worker.ts'], bundle: true, format: 'esm', platform: 'neutral',
  mainFields: ['module', 'main'], target: 'es2022',
  conditions: ['workerd', 'worker', 'browser', 'import', 'module', 'default'],
  plugins: [collect, sentryOrchestrionPlugin()],
};
await esbuild.build({ ...common, outfile: 'dist/probe.mjs' });   // pass 1: discover builtins
const names = [...used].sort();
const banner = [
  ...names.map((n, i) => `import * as __nb${i} from "node:${n}";`),
  `const __nbMap = { ${names.map((n, i) => `"${n}": __nb${i}`).join(', ')} };`,
  'globalThis.require = id => { const m = __nbMap[String(id).replace(/^node:/, "")];',
  '  if (!m) throw new Error("Cannot find module " + id);',
  '  return m.default !== undefined ? m.default : m; };',
].join('\n');
await esbuild.build({ ...common, outfile: 'dist/worker.mjs', banner: { js: banner } });
```

`deno task build && node build-worker.mjs && npx wrangler dev`. Use `mysql@2`; `mysql2` produces spans but its query then throws `EvalError: Code generation from strings disallowed for this context` in workerd.

